ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":98,"prev":31,"next":99,"titles":101,"firmware":25},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":10,"order":11,"path":12,"context":13,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":26,"procedures":55,"parameters":78,"related":79,"body":85,"sources":86,"official_url":30,"controls":94},"players.overview","Players",[5,6,7,8,9],"player","player key","note player","player type","player style","players",0,"knowledge/manual/units/players/overview.md",{"modes":14,"screens":17},[15,16],"instrument","auxiliary",[5],"A player reworks the notes a track plays — into arpeggios, transposed chords (maestro) or latched notes (hold) — and is switched on per track with the player key.","outdated-in-guide",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":24,"verified_on":25},"1.0.9",[23],"1.1.25","1.1.15","1.1.33",[27,33,36,41,44,47,51],{"id":28,"text":29,"source":30,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":31,"confidence":32},"what","A player takes the notes a track receives, from the keyboard or its sequence, and turns them into a variation such as an arpeggio or a chord hit; the recorded notes stay as they are.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/players#players",null,"official",{"id":34,"text":35,"source":30,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":31,"confidence":32},"tracks","Every instrument track and every auxiliary track can run a player of its own.",{"id":37,"text":38,"source":39,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":25,"confidence":40},"enable","The first press of `player` shows the selected track's player page, dimmed under an off box; a second press switches the player on.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#27-players","verified",{"id":42,"text":43,"source":39,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":25,"confidence":40},"types","`shift + player` opens the player list, headed with the track number and the word player: arpeggio, hold and maestro, the current type boxed.",{"id":45,"text":46,"source":39,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":25,"confidence":40},"list-steps","With the list up and shift still held, turning `E1` moves the box between arpeggio, hold and maestro; pressing `player` again only switches the player on or off. Letting go of shift opens the chosen player's page.",{"id":48,"text":49,"source":50,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":31,"confidence":32},"no-locks","Player settings cannot be parameter-locked; only module-page parameters can.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sequencer#step-sequencing",{"id":52,"text":53,"source":54,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":31,"confidence":32},"new-pattern","Since OS 1.1.25, a pattern you add to a track starts out with the player type that is selected at that moment.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.25",[56,66],{"id":37,"goal":57,"preconditions":58,"steps":61,"result":31,"source":30,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":31,"confidence":32},"Switch on a player for the selected track",[59,60],"instrument or auxiliary mode","the track is selected",[62,64],{"keys":5,"note":63,"set":31},"opens the player page",{"keys":5,"note":65,"set":31},"switches the player on",{"id":67,"goal":68,"preconditions":69,"steps":70,"result":77,"source":39,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":25,"confidence":40},"change-type","Choose another player type",[],[71,74],{"keys":72,"note":73,"set":31},"shift + player","opens the list with the current type boxed; keep shift held",{"keys":75,"note":76,"set":31},"shift + player → + turn E1","`E1` moves the box to arpeggio, hold or maestro; pressing player again would only switch the player on or off","Letting go of shift opens the chosen player's page.",[],[80,81,82,83,84],"players.arpeggio","players.maestro","players.hold","arrange.patterns","sequencer.parameter-locks","Players sit between what you play and what the track sounds: the arpeggio spells a chord out note\nby note, maestro plays whole chords from one finger, and hold keeps notes ringing after you let go.\nThe sequence is untouched, so switching the player off brings the original notes back. Since new\npatterns copy the current player type (1.1.25), the type seems to belong to the pattern.",[87,89,91,92],{"url":30,"kind":88},"guide",{"url":39,"kind":90},"research",{"url":50,"kind":88},{"url":54,"kind":93},"changelog",[95,96,97],"key.player","key.shift","encoder.1",{"id":10,"title":3},{"id":80,"title":100},"Arpeggio player",{"basics.key-notation":102,"basics.main-modes":103,"basics.modules":104,"basics.track-buttons":105,"basics.linked-tracks":106,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":107,"basics.workflow":108,"basics.firmware-versions":109,"hardware.layout":110,"hardware.power-and-charging":111,"hardware.connectors":112,"hardware.specifications":113,"hardware.te-boot":114,"hardware.firmware-update":115,"hardware.factory-reset":116,"hardware.system-menu":117,"hardware.safety-and-care":118,"hardware.in-the-box":119,"sequencer.overview":120,"sequencer.step-entry":121,"sequencer.step-recording":122,"sequencer.live-recording":123,"sequencer.extend-notes":124,"sequencer.nudge":125,"sequencer.single-sound":126,"sequencer.rotate":127,"sequencer.copy-step":128,"sequencer.transpose-sequence":129,"sequencer.parameter-locks":130,"sequencer.clear-and-undo":131,"sequencer.step-components":132,"sequencer.step-component-reference":133,"sequencer.component-pulse":134,"sequencer.component-pulse-hold":135,"sequencer.component-multiply":136,"sequencer.component-velocity":137,"sequencer.component-ramp-up":138,"sequencer.component-ramp-down":139,"sequencer.component-random":140,"sequencer.component-portamento":141,"sequencer.component-bend":142,"sequencer.component-tonality":143,"sequencer.component-jump":144,"sequencer.component-skip-parameter-lock":145,"sequencer.component-skip-step-component":146,"sequencer.component-skip-trigger":147,"sequencer.bar-menu":148,"sequencer.track-scale":149,"sequencer.bars-and-length":150,"players.overview":3,"players.arpeggio":100,"players.maestro":151,"players.hold":152,"instrument.overview":153,"instrument.engine":154,"instrument.envelopes":155,"instrume